# This file exists so `openspec/proposals/` survives empty periods
# (between the last proposal archiving and the next being opened).
# Without it, git would clean up the empty directory and references
# to the path would break.
#
# Current consumers of the directory path (as of 2026-05-17):
#   - scripts/openspec-triage.sh — looks for proposal directories
#     under openspec/proposals/YYYY-MM-DD-*/ in PR diffs.
#   - team-os/openspec-policy.md — describes openspec/proposals/ as
#     the lifecycle home for in-flight proposals.
#   - standards/openspec-standard.md — defines the directory layout.
#   - openspec/README.md — the OpenSpec entrypoint that lists current
#     and archived proposals; mentions the proposals/ directory.
#
# Do not delete this file as cruft. If you need to remove it (e.g.,
# because openspec/proposals/ should never be empty in a future
# convention), update the references above first.
